Instantiating a C++ abstract class and a GDScript abstract class.

<img width="3820" height="2039" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbf213b7-9000-4b88-beb5-23edcbae5924" />

The C++ class is correctly registered with Godot.

<img width="1952" height="1141" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f153513-3fd4-4c9b-bc3b-681f4a09ccf3" />

The godot-cpp function that appears responsible for correctly defining the creation function nullptr if it is abstract.
```cpp
// class_db.hpp
template <typename T>
	static GDExtensionObjectPtr _create_instance_func(void *data, GDExtensionBool p_notify_postinitialize) {
		if constexpr (!std::is_abstract_v<T>) {
			Wrapped::_set_construct_info<T>();
			T *new_object = new ("", "") T;
			if (p_notify_postinitialize) {
				new_object->_postinitialize();
			}
			return new_object->_owner;
		} else {
			return nullptr;
		}
	}
```

### Steps to reproduce

1) Fresh install of Godot from Arch pacman `sudo pacman -Syu godot`
2) Follow the example of setting up [godot-cpp GDExtension](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.html) (godot-cpp version used is 4.5)
3) Create the C++ abstract class and register it with Godot

C++ Abstract Class:
```cpp
// foo.h
#pragma once
#include "godot_cpp/classes/ref_counted.hpp"

namespace godot {
    class MyAbstractClass : public RefCounted
    {
        GDCLASS(MyAbstractClass, RefCounted)
    public:
        virtual bool pure_virtual() = 0;
        int get_number() { return 42; }
    protected:
        static void _bind_methods();
    };
}

// foo.cpp
#include "foo.h"
#include <godot_cpp/core/class_db.hpp>

void MyAbstractClass::_bind_methods()
{
    ClassDB::bind_method(D_METHOD("get_number"), &MyAbstractClass::get_number);
}
```

C++ Class Registration:
```cpp
// register_types.cpp
#include "register_types.h"

#include <gdextension_interface.h>
#include <godot_cpp/core/defs.hpp>
#include <godot_cpp/godot.hpp>

#include "foo.h"

using namespace godot;

void initialize_module(ModuleInitializationLevel p_level) {
	if (p_level != MODULE_INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SCENE) {
		return;
	}

	ClassDB::register_abstract_class<MyAbstractClass>();
}
```
4) Create a GDScript script and attach it to the scene

GDScript Function:
```GDScript
extends Node


# Called when the node enters the scene tree for the first time.
func _ready() -> void:
	# C++ version
	var my_abstract_cpp: MyAbstractClass = MyAbstractClass.new()
	print(str(my_abstract_cpp.get_number()))

	# GDScript version
	var my_abstract_gdscript: script_abstract = script_abstract.new()
	print(str(my_abstract_gdscript.get_number()))
	pass # Replace with function body.


# Called every frame. 'delta' is the elapsed time since the previous frame.
func _process(delta: float) -> void:
	pass

@abstract
class script_abstract:
	extends RefCounted

	func get_number() -> int:
		return 42
```
5) An error for the GDScript defined abstract class will be produced but there will be no error for the C++ version

